  "review": {
    "book": "JDG",
    "entityID": "person:amorite_237",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:34",
        "textualBasisJa": "The Amorites forced the children of Dan into the hill country, for they would not allow them to come down to the valley;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:35",
        "textualBasisJa": "but the Amorites would dwell in Mount Heres, in Aijalon, and in Shaalbim. Yet the hand of the house of Joseph prevailed, so that they became subject to forced labor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 1:36",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border of the Amorites was from the ascent of Akrabbim, from the rock, and upward."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 3:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Israel lived among the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 6:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "I said to you, “I am the LORD your God. You shall not fear the gods of the Amorites, in whose land you dwell.” But you have not listened to my voice.’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 10:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "They troubled and oppressed the children of Israel that year. For eighteen years they oppressed all the children of Israel that were beyond the Jordan in the land of the Amorites, which is in Gilead."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 10:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD said to the children of Israel, “Didn’t I save you from the Egyptians, and from the Amorites, from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 11:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, the king of Heshbon; and Israel said to him, ‘Please let us pass through your land to my place.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 11:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD, the God of Israel, delivered Sihon and all his people into the hand of Israel, and they struck them. So Israel possessed all the land of the Amorites, the inhabitants of that country."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 11:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "They possessed all the border of the Amorites, from the Arnon even to the Jabbok, and from the wilderness even to the Jordan."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 11:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "So now the LORD, the God of Israel, has dispossessed the Amorites from before his people Israel, and should you possess them?"
      }
    ],
